{
  "work_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies",
  "source_path": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies.json",
  "source_language": "cop",
  "target_language": "eng",
  "provenance": {
    "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12": {
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "prompt_version": "bulk-2026-10-12",
      "date": "2026-10-12",
      "script": "scripts.embed_eval.translate"
    }
  },
  "translations": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.000.0000",
      "source_sha256": "8d5ad5270f17a582",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "Likewise, a homily delivered in Constantinople, in the church of Anthemius, by Proclus, bishop of Cyzicus, on the Sunday of Absolution, when they seated him on the archbishop’s throne, while Nestorius the heretic was present."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.000.0004",
      "source_sha256": "803679d09fb37863",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "What mind has ever thought in this way before?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.000.0023",
      "source_sha256": "67ffee78ce8605a3",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "He raised up the temple that he had willingly destroyed through death."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.000.0046",
      "source_sha256": "479604fe255c15c8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "On what day? Tell us, O prophet!"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.000.0060",
      "source_sha256": "d3d6d3e38c627f17",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "Death cannot dare to swallow the incorruptible divine nature."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.000.0062",
      "source_sha256": "1f4f14a05f2c0f8f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "For he is the one whom the seraphim do not see."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.000.0092",
      "source_sha256": "3be3f76d2bf30470",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "Tell us, O temple, why did the curtain tear when they were about to crucify Christ?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0006",
      "source_sha256": "3a25954f5d3d2956",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "The wealth of the Savior’s gifts is beyond words."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0007",
      "source_sha256": "6878ac0198855373",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "It is ungrudging, and great is the treasury of gifts stored up in heaven."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0008",
      "source_sha256": "ba1cddbcf984c5fe",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "This grace knows no poverty, for Christ is the one who gives this grace. And if you wish, beloved, look at the holy Scriptures, and you will know the immeasurable wealth with which he gives great gifts."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0009",
      "source_sha256": "6ca812ed64ee5427",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "For he wishes to show it to you precisely: it is without limit and manifold in its ways."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0010",
      "source_sha256": "091023d8e89ce41e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "For from the beginning, our Lord Jesus Christ does not cease doing good to the human race."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0019",
      "source_sha256": "ef3346aa8902536d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "He rebuked the disobedient Balaam through a donkey, making his animal rational instead of irrational."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0020",
      "source_sha256": "9981c98cc6891507",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "For a useful purpose, he granted understanding to the Red Sea."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0021",
      "source_sha256": "c58446fbffd5ac1c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "He made Aaron’s staff become the mother of a new shoot, contrary to its nature."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0022",
      "source_sha256": "b2cd5d2b6c5becfe",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "He set up a bronze serpent in the wilderness as a wondrous means of healing."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0023",
      "source_sha256": "cf040d9ad3667411",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "He saw Elijah fleeing, took him up, and made him a citizen of heaven."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0048",
      "source_sha256": "3bfcdc401cb11f3b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "For the one who exists did not come into being."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0049",
      "source_sha256": "9310cde41316ea95",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "For the one who came into being is not a phantom."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0052",
      "source_sha256": "e2b46a0cec5d7cd0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "We do not divide the natures into two hypostases. Rather, the two natures constitute one single hypostasis, from divinity and the humanity of the wondrous dispensation, which became one with him. After the indescribable union, he exists as the only-begotten Son."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0064",
      "source_sha256": "c562c154892058e2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "He is life, because in him we live and exist and move."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0078",
      "source_sha256": "7b32129cc17eb42b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "Then he is a door, because he is the guide into paradise."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0091",
      "source_sha256": "cc5fb14abadb5790",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "For he took a body, a soul, and a mind, so that through them he might accept death and redeem us from it."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "patristic/coptic-scriptorium/proclus_homilies#CopScr.proclus-homilies.001.0105",
      "source_sha256": "94aa18e307d3b647",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-12",
      "group_size": 24,
      "text": "The rush of the winds, or its fierceness."
    }
  ]
}
